<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Udayana of Vatsa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">6th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Udayana was a king of Vatsa, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kausambi">Kaushambi</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yamuna">Yamuna</a>, in the 6th century BCE, a contemporary of the Buddha. Buddhist texts and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> drama make him a romantic hero: his capture by King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pradyota">Pradyota</a> of Avanti and his elopement with Pradyota's daughter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vasavadatta">Vasavadatta</a> are the subject of plays such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhasa">Bhasa</a>'s Svapnavasavadattam. His reign marks the height of Vatsa as one of the great kingdoms.</p></div>
